Subject: Fix RCCL device linking on memory-constrained builders
Origin: Debian, https://sources.debian.org/patches/rccl/7.2.4-1~exp3/rccl-launchpad-build-fix.patch/
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/rccl/+bug/2149786
Author: Bojan Aleksovski <bojan.aleksovski@canonical.com>
Last-Update: 2026-04-16

Reduce device LTO and code generation optimization to O1 and use a
single LTO partition to limit build time and memory pressure.
The linker flags are unchanged from the Debian/Ubuntu patch.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1344,6 +1344,10 @@ if (HAVE_KERNARG_PRELOAD)
   target_link_options(rccl PRIVATE "SHELL:-Xoffload-linker -mllvm=-amdgpu-kernarg-preload-count=16")
 endif()
 
+target_link_options(rccl PRIVATE "SHELL:-Xoffload-linker --lto-O1")
+target_link_options(rccl PRIVATE "SHELL:-Xoffload-linker --lto-CGO1")
+target_link_options(rccl PRIVATE "SHELL:-Xoffload-linker --lto-partitions=1")
+
 if(ENABLE_MSCCLPP)
   include(cmake/MSCCLPP.cmake)
 endif()
